sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch07-05> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch07-05--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch07-05--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch07-05: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.62" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.621"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/mixed" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.66"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The quantitative core is an amplification count from public atomic and thermal scales, and a doubling map reaches atomic lengths in a few tens of steps, which a small team can recompute. Raw trajectories of the pegboard, kneading, and mirror devices are not a public dataset, so the laboratory half is a scaling argument rather than a reanalysis of runs. Around ten and typically remain order-of-magnitude statements tied to apparatus size." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Count e-foldings between a stated macroscopic tolerance and an atomic or thermal scale, using a doubling per collision or per kneading step. A result of order ten collisions for a laboratory-scale pegboard would support that clause; a separation of hundreds of collisions would challenge it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Around ten depends on the size of the apparatus and the initial uncertainty.", "A real pegboard also has fabrication error, not only atomic uncertainty.", "Kneading and mirror arrangements are idealized, so only the scale-separation arithmetic is directly calculable." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch07-05--grok--dataset-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch07-05--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of wolfram2002-ch07-05 by Grok 4.7: 0.7" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch07-05--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch07-05> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch07-05--grok--operationalizability> .
